# Redoubt isolation-media-process.patch  (Android, OVERLAY isolation-media)
# Owner: LW-M7-50 ("Isolated content with MediaCodec in RDD: prototype behind a
# build switch"), follow-up of the LW-M7-48 study (docs/android/ISOLATION-MEDIA-STUDY.md)
#
# Applied ONLY by `scripts/librewolf-patches.py --overlays=isolation-media`
# (Makefile: OVERLAYS=isolation-media), from assets/patches/overlay-isolation-media.txt,
# after every patch in android.txt. A normal build never applies it, so its
# tree is the one patches/android/isolated-process.patch leaves: isolation OFF.
#
# Owner decisions 2026-10-10, verbatim:
#   plan        "Prototype now, ship ON in a 158 dot release if it tests clean"
#   trade-off   "Keep software codecs in the page process"
#   testing     "Yes, separate dev app"
#
# Upstream file touched
# ---------------------
#   mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
#
# The two literals that isolated-process.patch (LW-M5-02, revised by LW-M7-43)
# pins to false go back to true: content runs in `isolatedTabN`/`zygoteTab`
# services, as u:r:isolated_app with its own isolated uid, forked from the app
# zygote, and cannot read the profile directory (isolated-process.patch,
# "How this was verified", items 1-2). They stay literals: no setting and no
# Nimbus value can lower them (isolated-process.patch, "Why the value is
# hard-coded").
#
# Why this is safe for video now: LW-M7-43 turned isolation off because an
# isolated content process has no H.264/HEVC/AAC decoder
# (AndroidDecoderModule::IsJavaDecoderModuleAllowed() is false there, bug
# 1810736). The same overlay sets upstream's eleven isolated-process media prefs
# (assets/patches/overlay-isolation-media.cfg, bug 1988531 part 1), which decode
# those codecs with ffvpx + the NDK MediaCodec in the RDD process (video) and the
# Utility process (audio), and keeps every software codec in the isolated
# content process (isolation-media-codecs-in-content.patch).
#
# Native HLS, decided: FAIL CLOSED, no workaround. HLSDecoder::IsEnabled() is
# `media_hls_enabled() && !GeckoAppShell::IsIsolatedProcess()`
# (dom/media/hls/HLSDecoder.cpp:360-363 in 158.0), because the ExoPlayer-based
# GeckoHlsPlayer cannot bind services from an isolated process (bug 2043165).
# So canPlayType("application/vnd.apple.mpegurl") is "" and a page whose ONLY
# source is a native <video src=".m3u8"> gets MEDIA_ERR_SRC_NOT_SUPPORTED
# (error 4). Any page that feature-detects (hls.js, video.js, Shaka, every
# major player) falls back to MSE, which plays H.264/AAC through RDD. No pref
# turns native HLS back on: re-enabling it would mean running ExoPlayer in a
# non-isolated process, which is design (b) of the study and rejected there.
# Measured in docs/android/evidence/lw-m7-50/.
#
# Ordering: must apply AFTER patches/android/isolated-process.patch (its context
# is that patch's comment block and literals). Guaranteed structurally, because
# overlay lists apply after android.txt, and recorded as a constraint in
# scripts/check-patch-order.py.
#
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/gecko/GeckoProvider.kt
@@ -158,8 +158,13 @@
                 // Turn this back on only after a Firefox release decodes H.264 from an
                 // isolated content process; the measurement is in
                 // docs/android/evidence/video-playback/README.md.
-                .isolatedProcessEnabled(false)
-                .appZygoteProcessEnabled(false)
+                // Redoubt LW-M7-50 (isolation-media overlay, opt-in build): back ON. H.264,
+                // HEVC and AAC are decoded by the NDK MediaCodec in the RDD/Utility process
+                // (prefs in assets/patches/overlay-isolation-media.cfg), so the isolated
+                // content process no longer needs the Java decoder module it cannot reach.
+                // Still literals, so no setting or experiment can turn them off.
+                .isolatedProcessEnabled(true)
+                .appZygoteProcessEnabled(true)
 
         if (FxNimbus.features.fission.value().shouldUseNimbus) {
             builder.fissionEnabled(FxNimbus.features.fission.value().enabled)
